    "Model exhibits severe underestimation during high-volatility regimes; true outcomes frequently spike 5-10% above forecasts when recent history shows a mix of highs and lows.",
    "Forecast fails to capture immediate mean reversion after sharp spikes; model predicts smooth linear growth while true data oscillates wildly around the forecast path.",
    "Sentiment signals (specifically +1.00) are ignored by the model, which continues its downward or flat trajectory despite positive market sentiment coinciding with price surges.",
    "Model displays significant lag in reacting to recent volatility; it assumes a stable trend while true outcomes react instantly to short-term sentiment shifts.",
    "In high-volatility periods, the model's 30-day horizon forecast is consistently biased toward the lower bound of the actual range, missing upper-bound spikes."
  ]
